      "id": 4,
      "claim": "By both acknowledging the band‑aid criticism (step 3) and asserting that backup duties still obligate us to donate, Ashford diffuses the criticism’s force.",
      "evidence": "Ashford’s argument uses the backup‑duty move to admit the limitation while preserving moral responsibility, thereby neutralising the charge that effective altruism is useless.",
      "weight": 0.25,
